{
  "id": "sparse_autoencoders_intro",
  "title": "Unlocking Polysemantic Neural Latents",
  "category": "mechanism_deepdive",
  "domain_taxonomy": "neural_sae",
  "hook_tag": "NEURAL SUPERPOSITION ARCHITECTURE",
  "beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": 1,
      "text": "How can a model track millions of features using a hidden dimension of only four thousand? The secret is neural superposition.",
      "visual_focus": "A dense vector space collapsing into a glowing, high-dimensional lattice.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "neural superposition": "#38BDF8"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Neural Latents",
        "action_verb": "collapse",
        "direct_object": "hidden dimensions",
        "anchor_word": "superposition",
        "semantic_role": "state_transition"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 2,
      "text": "Dense layers are bottlenecked by interference. Features overlap in polysemantic vectors, making individual neurons impossible to interpret or isolate effectively.",
      "visual_focus": "Intertwined, blurry overlapping color clouds showing chaotic interference.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "interference": "#EF4444",
        "polysemantic": "#EF4444"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "Dense Weights",
        "action_verb": "entangle",
        "direct_object": "feature activations",
        "anchor_word": "interference",
        "semantic_role": "causal_elimination"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 3,
      "text": "Sparse Autoencoders solve this by projecting latent activations into a massive, expanded dictionary of over-complete, monosemantic feature directions.",
      "visual_focus": "A single vector expanding into a wide, structured dictionary array.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "Sparse Autoencoders": "#34D399",
        "monosemantic": "#34D399"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "SAE Encoder",
        "action_verb": "projects",
        "direct_object": "latent activations",
        "anchor_word": "projecting",
        "semantic_role": "agent_action"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 4,
      "text": "We apply an L1 penalty to the latent vector, forcing the model to select only the most relevant, non-zero feature activations.",
      "visual_focus": "A threshold filter gating a stream of activation values.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "L1 penalty": "#F59E0B",
        "non-zero": "#F59E0B"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "L1 Gate",
        "action_verb": "prunes",
        "direct_object": "non-zero latents",
        "anchor_word": "pruning",
        "semantic_role": "causal_elimination"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 5,
      "text": "This yields ninety-eight percent recovery of internal states, effectively untangling the model without sacrificing performance or compute efficiency.",
      "visual_focus": "Two charts showing recovered features aligning perfectly with ground truth.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "ninety-eight percent": "#34D399"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "SAE Decoder",
        "action_verb": "reconstructs",
        "direct_object": "original activations",
        "anchor_word": "recovery",
        "semantic_role": "metric_evaluation"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": 6,
      "text": "Follow The Model Verse for the engineering behind modern AI architectures.",
      "visual_focus": "The Model Verse logo fades in against a clean chalkboard grid.",
      "highlight_words": {
        "The Model Verse": "#34D399"
      },
      "svo_action": {
        "subject": "The Model Verse",
        "action_verb": "reveals",
        "direct_object": "architectural engineering",
        "anchor_word": "Follow",
        "semantic_role": "agent_action"
      }
    }
  ],
  "math_formulas": [
